llvm-mos-65816: WRAM write watch for bsnes-jg 2.1.0 (pinned; src/cpu.cpp sha256 9c3fa4a17e0c6386ad01b7e040ccbfafa4971b4d1288e52ddd30b953c4dbbcee).

Calls jgx_wram_watch_cb(offset, data, pc) after every CPU/DMA write whose WRAM offset lies in
[jgx_wram_watch_lo, +jgx_wram_watch_len). The window defaults to empty (one compare per WRAM write).
dev/jgxcheck.cpp (tools/stackguard.h) arms it on __rc0/__rc1 to track the lowest soft-stack pointer.
Applied by dev/xcheck.sh; dev/build-cycle-probe.py copies the patched tree and its needles are untouched.

--- a/src/cpu.cpp
+++ b/src/cpu.cpp
@@ -31,6 +31,16 @@
 
 #include "cpu.hpp"
 
+// llvm-mos-65816 WRAM write watch (dev/bsnes-jg-wramwatch.patch). A harness sets
+// [jgx_wram_watch_lo, +jgx_wram_watch_len) and jgx_wram_watch_cb; every CPU/DMA write whose WRAM
+// offset (0..0x1FFFF) falls inside the window then calls cb(offset, data, pc) after wram[] is
+// updated. The default window is empty, so the cost to everything else is one compare per write.
+extern "C" {
+  unsigned jgx_wram_watch_lo = 0;
+  unsigned jgx_wram_watch_len = 0;
+  void (*jgx_wram_watch_cb)(unsigned offset, uint8_t data, uint32_t pc) = nullptr;
+}
+
 namespace SuperFamicom {
 
 CPU cpu;
@@ -445,6 +455,7 @@
 
 void CPU::writeRAM(unsigned addr, uint8_t data) {
   wram[addr] = data;
+  if(addr - jgx_wram_watch_lo < jgx_wram_watch_len) jgx_wram_watch_cb(addr, data, r.pc.d);
 }
 
